# Astroberry OS 3.2 components, installed from Astroberry's APT repository.
#
# This is the dependency list of the `astroberry-os` meta-package with
# KStars (kstars-bleeding) left out, because KStars/EKOS is not required here
# and the meta-package cannot be installed without it. The packages themselves
# are Astroberry's, unmodified. Revisit this list when astroberry-os changes:
#   apt-cache depends astroberry-os
#
# Core: web interface, system modifications (hotspot, remote desktop, file
# sharing, Caddy), INDI drivers, PHD2, star catalogue and solvers.
astroberry-manager
astroberry-os-sysmod
indi-3rdparty-drivers
gsc
astrometry.net
astap
phd2
phdlogview
# Desktop session used by the remote desktop.
xfce4
xfce4-goodies
xfce4-power-manager
xfce4-terminal
lightdm
dbus-x11
firefox-esr
network-manager-applet
nm-connection-editor
synaptic
# Astroberry's other astronomy applications. firecapture, astrodmx-capture and
# ccdciel are third-party binaries in Astroberry's `restricted` component, which
# the documented `main`-only repository setup does not enable; omitted here.
gpredict
ser-player
siril
# Administration access for the smoke test.
openssh-server
# Installer. Calamares copies this live system (Astroberry included) to disk and
# adds an "Install Debian" launcher to the live desktop. It needs the bootloader
# packages present to install GRUB on BIOS and UEFI machines.
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
grub-efi-amd64-signed
shim-signed
efibootmgr
os-prober
# Firmware. live-build's automatic firmware list (--firmware-chroot) is turned
# off because it adds every package tagged as firmware, including indi-dsi, which
# conflicts with Astroberry's indi-3rdparty-drivers. These cover common Wi-Fi
# adapters (the hotspot needs one) and CPU microcode.
firmware-linux
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-misc-nonfree
wireless-regdb
amd64-microcode
intel-microcode
